Day 61 /100 of #DrGViswanathanChallenge

Today, I solved LeetCode 1008 -(Construct Binary Search Tree from Preorder Traversal.)
- Approach:
I used recursion with a boundary (max value) to construct the BST efficiently.
The first element of the preorder traversal becomes the root.
Maintain an index i to track the current element.
If i reaches the end of the array or the current value exceeds the allowed upper bound, return null.
Create a node using preorder[i] and increment i.
Recursively construct the left subtree with the current node's value as the upper bound.
Recursively construct the right subtree using the previous upper bound.
Since preorder traversal visits root → left → right, this naturally allows us to reconstruct the BST.

- Time Complexity: O(N) Each element is processed only once.
-Space Complexity:O(H) Due to the recursive call stack, where H is the height of the BST.

-Key Takeaways
1) Strengthened my understanding of BST properties
2) Learned how preorder traversal can be used to reconstruct a BST
3) Practiced using upper bounds in recursion
4) Understood how a single index can efficiently process the entire array
5) Improved my understanding of recursive tree construction
